  "difficulty": "tutorial",
  "description": "The bottling line needs its control signal one tick later. Conduits carry a charge through an entire welded wire in the same tick; a Delay Gate copies its rear input to its front output on the next tick, preserving +1, -1, and 0. Select a Delay Gate, press D to point it right, and place it between the fixed INPUT and OUTPUT wires. Fill the gaps with conduits and weld every touching pair along the path; hold Control to weld without changing tools. The fixed machinery compares your OUTPUT against EXPECTED on every tick, so a plain wire or two gates in series will fail. Watch the three signal traces, then use Test to pass both sequences.",
  "goal": "Reproduce every input charge exactly one tick later, including zeros.",
